<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The paperclip module's prompts: the text Metaform sends to agents, and to people, for the paperclip module.
     Each element is one prompt, named by its tag. What is between the tags is sent exactly as written; an empty
     element inside a prompt marks a place the code fills in. Comments are never sent.
     The issue document the module keeps on each Paperclip issue, keyed metaform, is data, one line each (address,
     brief, ticket), and is not written here. What is written here is the prose Paperclip's people and agents read on
     an issue's thread, and the questions Jev is asked. -->
<prompts>
<!-- paperclip's line in the connect message: one short phrase saying what an agent uses the module for, written
     after the module's name, '– paperclip: <what it is for>', in the project's terms. Sent to every agent when it
     connects over MCP, one line per enabled module under mcp's <instructions>, and listed in the compact
     command-line guide, metaform help agents. Empty, as here, sends nothing: the person writes it. Off until the
     module is enabled, and when the folder's modules setting leaves it out. -->
<connect></connect>
<!-- paperclip's instructions. Returned by metaform_instructions with module paperclip, at
     metaform://instructions/paperclip, and printed by metaform help agents paperclip and by the full form of the
     command-line guide. Empty sends nothing. Off until the module is enabled. -->
<instructions>paperclip is active.</instructions>
<!-- The line under the counts an agent is told at its node, MCP-039. paperclip declares no node_count, so this is
     never shown. -->
<counts></counts>
<!-- paperclip's rules, MCP-031, gathered at the end of metaform://tools, each "[paperclip] <rule> Why: <why>".
     Write each as <rule why="the reason">One sentence.</rule>. Empty, as here, sends nothing. -->
<rules></rules>
<!-- The comment `heartbeat` posts on a Paperclip issue it takes for a Metaform agent, once, in the same heartbeat.
     Read by the issue's people and by Paperclip's agents on its thread; Paperclip's heartbeat protocol asks for a
     comment on work left in progress (docs/guides/agent-developer/heartbeat-protocol.md). The places: <ticket/> the
     ticket's reference, <address>#<n>; <address/> the Address; <state/> one of the two sentences of <taken_state>
     below; <minutes/> how often Paperclip wakes the agent to check, the setting paperclip_check_minutes. Through
     Paperclip's tool gateway the map_where tool is named mcp.<connection>:map-where, since the gateway turns _ into -
     (server/src/services/tool-gateway.ts). Change the words freely; it cannot be turned off, since Paperclip treats
     an in-progress issue with no comment and no monitor as a stuck run. -->
<taken>Taken by Metaform as ticket <ticket/> at <address/>. <state/> Its brief is read with Metaform's map_where tool (map-where through Paperclip's tool gateway) and the address <address/>. Comments here are written at that Address for the person, and the questions asked there for this ticket come here to be answered. Paperclip wakes this agent every <minutes/> minutes to check until the ticket ends.</taken>
<!-- The <state/> of <taken>: <started> when dispatch's Autostart is on and heartbeat has asked dispatch to start the
     ticket's agent, <waiting> when Autostart is off and the ticket waits in To do for the person. -->
<taken_state>
<started>Metaform's dispatch starts an agent on it.</started>
<waiting>It waits for the person to start it in Metaform.</waiting>
</taken_state>
<!-- The comment `heartbeat` posts, once, on a Paperclip issue assigned to the Metaform agent that it cannot take
     because no Address is named for it and Jev chose none. Paperclip asks a run woken for an assignment to leave a
     comment, and retries the run once when it does not (server/src/services/heartbeat/queue.ts). `metaform paperclip
     link` is not offered here: it ties an issue a Paperclip agent works, which heartbeat then leaves alone. The
     place: <issue/> the issue's identifier. -->
<unrouted>Metaform could not tell where in the map <issue/>'s work lands. Add the line address: &lt;address&gt; to this issue's document keyed metaform, naming the Address it works on; the next heartbeat takes it.</unrouted>
<!-- The comment `sync` posts on a Paperclip issue when the Metaform ticket working it ends, with the issue's status
     set in the same call: done, cancelled, or in_review for a failed ticket, which also gets the <failed> question.
     The places: <ticket/> the ticket's reference; <outcome/> completed, cancelled or failed; <resolution/> the
     ticket's resolution as the agent wrote it. -->
<ended>Metaform ticket <ticket/> ended <outcome/>: <resolution/></ended>
<!-- The question card `sync` puts on a Paperclip issue whose Metaform ticket failed, as an ask_user_questions
     interaction only a person may answer, so the issue waits in in_review on a real path (skills/paperclip/SKILL.md:
     "Human-input waits use a saved pending interaction and in_review"). <title> is the card's title, <ask> its
     question; <retry> and <close> are its two answers: retry moves the issue to todo, and the next heartbeat takes it
     as a new ticket at the same Address; close cancels the issue. The places: <ticket/> the ticket's reference;
     <address/> the Address; <resolution/> the ticket's resolution. -->
<failed>
<title>Metaform ticket <ticket/> failed</title>
<ask>Metaform ticket <ticket/> at <address/> ended failed: <resolution/> What should happen to this issue?</ask>
<retry>Try again: Metaform takes it as a new ticket at the same Address.</retry>
<close>Close it: cancel this issue.</close>
</failed>
<!-- The title of the map message `sync` writes at a ticket's Address for each comment on its Paperclip issue, so the
     Metaform agent working the ticket reads what Paperclip's people and agents said; the message's text is the comment
     as written. The places: <issue/> the issue's identifier, such as PAP-12; <author/> who wrote it, agent or person
     and their Paperclip id. -->
<comment>Comment on <issue/> from <author/></comment>
<!-- What Jev is asked when a Paperclip issue assigned to the Metaform agent names no Address in its metaform document:
     which of the map's Addresses its work lands on. Asked only when the setting jev is on and paperclip_jev_route is
     on; a sure answer is kept at the chosen Address as a numbered item, metaform://<address>#<n>, and the issue is
     taken there; any other answer leaves the issue as it is. <title> and <why> name the kept decision; <ask> is the
     question Jev reads, about the state's `issue` and `addresses`; <none> is the way out, what it means that no
     Address fits. The place: <issue/> the issue's identifier. -->
<jev_route>
<title>Address for Paperclip issue <issue/></title>
<why>A Paperclip issue is worked at one Address, so the agent reads that node's brief and leaves what it learns there.</why>
<ask>Which Address in `addresses` is the part of the work that the Paperclip issue in `issue` asks to be changed, judged by what each Address's purposes say?</ask>
<none>None of these Addresses is where this issue's work lands, or the issue is too vague to tell.</none>
</jev_route>
</prompts>
